Q: Spring Boot 4 with Kotlin - Jackson deserialization problems A: <p>Can you try this? Since a few Kotlin versions I got the warning that you have to decide where you want to put the annotation on: constructor parameter or the field itself.</p>
<pre><code>data class AuthenticationRequest(
        @param:JsonProperty
        val username : String,
        @param:JsonProperty
        val password : String
)

// alternative

data class AuthenticationRequest(
        @field:JsonProperty
        val username : String,
        @field:JsonProperty
        val password : String
)
</code></pre>
